note E14 dominating-check rule, boundary (positive): put t i 1 on a 32-byte local checks i < 32, so the secret
note store to c[i] is in 0..31, one byte below the declared count field [32,40). With e14 it is excused
note (bounded-offset). An off-by-one in the refinement (i <= 32) would admit c[32] and revoke the field.
fn f c edit uchar 104 a view uchar 1 i ulong to ulong
t = new uchar 32 0
put t i 1
put c i get a 0
if eq get c 32 0
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
